Interaction-mode reminder in the prelude instead of the system prompt

The main session's system prompt ended with 'Interaction mode reminder: You
are running as <role>. <question guidance>', so headless, interactive and ACP
prompts differed at the end of the system prompt, which providers that cache
per prefix checkpoint (end of system prompt + tools) cannot share. The main
session now sends that reminder as the first part of its startup prelude
(also after /clear and auto-compaction) and its system prompt is identical in
every mode. Other users of getCoreSystemPrompt (Arena agents) keep the
reminder in the system prompt; a configured or QWEN_SYSTEM_MD prompt gets
none, as before.

